WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.522
Use this guide to decide what kind of action the evidence supports.

00:00:03.522 --> 00:00:06.297
A known formatting difference can be standardized.

00:00:06.297 --> 00:00:09.877
A documented blank-as-missing convention can be normalized.

00:00:09.877 --> 00:00:13.807
An invalid value with unknown truth should be flagged or quarantined.

00:00:13.807 --> 00:00:19.877
Possible duplicates need detection and resolution logic.

00:00:19.877 --> 00:00:20.992
A supported correction can be applied safely.

00:00:20.992 --> 00:00:25.122
And stable rules can become constraints for future prevention.

00:00:25.122 --> 00:00:29.487
Connect this idea to a healthcare pipeline validating contact, demographic, and event fields.

00:00:29.487 --> 00:00:36.477
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:36.477 --> 00:00:41.632
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:41.632 --> 00:00:46.842
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:46.842 --> 00:00:52.000
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
